    <h2>2. Project Installation Instructions (MANDATORY)</h2>

    <h3>System Requirements:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>PHP 8.2 or 8.3 with extensions enabled: <code>pdo_mysql</code>, <code>pdo_sqlite</code>, <code>curl</code>, <code>mbstring</code>, <code>fileinfo</code>, <code>gd</code>, <code>openssl</code></li>
        <li>Composer (PHP Dependency Manager)</li>
        <li>XAMPP (Apache + MySQL) or standalone PHP development server</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Quick Setup Steps:</h3>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Open Terminal / Command Prompt</strong> and navigate into the extracted <code>MarketLink</code> directory:
            <br><code>cd MarketLink</code>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Install Dependencies:</strong>
            <br><code>composer install</code>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Environment Configuration:</strong>
            <br>Copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code> (if not already created) and generate an application key:
            <br><code>copy .env.example .env</code>
            <br><code>php artisan key:generate</code>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Database Options:</strong>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Option A (SQLite Instant Execution — Recommended):</strong>
                    <br>Run: <code>php artisan migrate:fresh --seed</code>
                    <br><em>(No MySQL setup needed; seeds all test accounts and produce automatically.)</em>
                </li>
                <li><strong>Option B (MySQL / XAMPP phpMyAdmin):</strong>
                    <br>1. Start Apache and MySQL in XAMPP.
                    <br>2. Open phpMyAdmin at <code>http://localhost/phpmyadmin</code>.
                    <br>3. Create a database named <code>marketlink</code>.
                    <br>4. Import the provided <code>marketlink.sql</code> script file.
                    <br>5. Update <code>.env</code> with <code>DB_CONNECTION=mysql</code>, <code>DB_DATABASE=marketlink</code>, <code>DB_USERNAME=root</code>.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Run Application:</strong>
            <br><code>php artisan serve</code>
            <br>Open your browser and navigate to: <strong><code>http://localhost:8000</code></strong>
        </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>3. Assumptions Made (SRS Section 1.9)</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Settlement at Stall Pickup:</strong> In strict conformance with SRS Section 1.5, pre-orders reserve inventory without online credit card transactions. Customers pay in person upon collecting their order.</li>
        <li><strong>Stall Geolocation Provider:</strong> OpenStreetMap (via Leaflet.js) was selected as authorized in SRS Section 1.8 to deliver reliable, open-access map markers and routing without external Google Maps billing limitations.</li>
        <li><strong>Cutoff Automation:</strong> Pre-orders lock automatically prior to the scheduled pickup time window (configured per farmer, default 2 hours) to allow growers adequate time for harvesting and packaging.</li>
        <li><strong>Verified Reviews:</strong> Reviews and star ratings are permitted exclusively after an order has reached the <code>completed</code> status, ensuring genuine feedback.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>4. Included SQL Script Files (SRS Section 1.9)</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><code>marketlink.sql</code> — Complete MySQL export including table schemas (DDL) and sample seed records (DML).</li>
    </ul>

